# Mosh App Store distribution exception

The Mosh developers are aware that the terms of service that apply to
apps distributed via Apple's App Store services may conflict with
rights granted under Mosh's license, the GNU General Public License,
version 3. The Mosh copyright holders do not wish this conflict to
prevent the otherwise-compliant distribution of Mosh-derived apps via
the App Store. Therefore, we have committed not to pursue any license
violation that results solely from the conflict between the GPLv3 and
the Apple App Store terms of service. In other words, as long as you
comply with the GPL in all other respects, including its requirements
to provide users with source code and the text of the license, we will
not object to your distribution of Mosh through the App Store.


# Tessera App Store distribution exception

Tessera's own source code is licensed under the GNU General Public
License, version 3, and the same conflict described above — between the
terms of the GPLv3 and the terms of service governing Apple's App Store
and TestFlight beta-distribution services — applies to it.

As an additional permission under section 7 of the GPLv3, Bambouville Inc.
grants permission for Tessera to be conveyed through Apple's App Store and
TestFlight only by Bambouville Inc. or by persons acting on Bambouville Inc.'s
behalf or with Bambouville Inc.'s prior written authorization.

For such official or authorized distribution, Bambouville Inc. will not treat
the distribution as a violation of the GPLv3 solely because Apple's App Store
or TestFlight terms impose conditions that would otherwise conflict with the
GPLv3, including the GPLv3 requirements regarding Installation Information for
User Products, to the extent Apple's platform makes those requirements
impossible to satisfy.

This additional permission does not apply to App Store or TestFlight
distribution by others. It does not restrict any rights under the GPLv3 to copy,
modify, or convey Tessera through channels whose terms allow full compliance
with the GPLv3. All other GPLv3 obligations remain, including the obligation to
provide Corresponding Source and the text of the License. Tessera satisfies the
source-availability requirement by publishing its complete corresponding source
at:

    https://github.com/bambouville/tessera

# Trademark reservation

As supplemental terms under sections 7(c) and 7(e) of the GPLv3, this license
does not grant any rights under trademark law to the "Tessera" name, the
Tessera app icon, or other Tessera brand assets, which identify the official
distribution by Bambouville Inc.

You must not misrepresent the origin of Tessera or any version of it. If you
convey a modified version, you must mark it as modified and must use a name,
icon, and branding that are reasonably distinguishable from the official
Tessera distribution and that do not suggest that Bambouville Inc. produced,
endorsed, or sponsors the modified version.

Nothing in this paragraph requires rebranding of unmodified, verbatim copies,
but no trademark rights are granted except to the extent permitted by applicable
trademark law.
